<title>GERMANY: German traders seek free mkt wheat, barley, rye.</title>
<headline>German traders seek free mkt wheat, barley, rye.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders are seeking export restitutions for the export of 4,000 tonnes of free market soft wheat in a range between 11.50 and 15.70 Ecus per tonne, state grain intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Traders at the weekly EU grain export tender also sought rebates for the export of 18,000 tonnes of free market barley in a 27.90-34.10 Ecus/tonne range.</p>
<p>They also sought rebates for 1,000 tonnes of rye at 31.45 Ecus.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
